8
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,260
want your agent to accomplish.

9
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:17,120
If you think about what has to fit

10
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,980
in there, that's just not enough

11
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:19,580
space

12
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:22,000
to tackle complex tasks in the real

13
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,600
world.

14
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:23,940
If this is going to work,

15
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,620
we need to understand the building

16
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:26,680
blocks of context

17
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:29,320
in modern agentic applications and

18
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,520
have a framework to help us design

19
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:33,580
context with precision.

20
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,120
Let me show you what I mean.

21
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,680
Let's remember what an LLM even is.

22
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:43,000
It's a stateless box that

23
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,560
takes tokens as input.

24
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,700
You just think of them as little

25
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,440
pieces of words and gives us,

26
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,400
we'll say,

27
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:54,300
likely tokens as outputs.

28
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,720
It's important to kind of bring back

29
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,960
to this core thing.

30
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,940
It's very smart, does a lot of

31
00:00:58,940 --> 00:00:59,540
really cool things.

32
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,240
These likely tokens are extremely

33
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,520
useful that come out, but it doesn't

34
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,240
remember anything.

35
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,100
We give it a bunch of text on the

36
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:09,240
input and text comes as the output

37
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,580
for the text mode.

38
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:13,000
When I said you have about a

39
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
million, that's for some models,

40
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:16,940
for some it might be 100,000,

41
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,040
something like that.

42
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,800
That could correspond to maybe 60

43
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,500
,000 words or 60 to 700,000 words,

44
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,100
